# The Sackville-Bagginses: "Whenever you sacrifice a token, target opponent loses 1 life." On turn 1 Bot1 casts Thraben
# Inspector, whose Clue token it sacrifices on turn 3 to the Sackville-Bagginses's own enters ability (it can: "another creature
# or artifact", and a Clue is an artifact). Bot1 draws a card and gets a Treasure; the sacrifice of the token triggers the second
# ability (the Sackville-Bagginses is on the battlefield by then) and Bot2 loses exactly 1 life. The Inspector stays.

[Bot1 Deck]
Plains
Swamp
Thraben Inspector
The Sackville-Bagginses
Island x12

[Bot2 Deck]
Island x20

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Plains.Play
Bot1.Battlefield.Plains.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Thraben Inspector.Cast
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Hand.Swamp.Play
Bot1.Battlefield.Plains.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Swamp.Activate
Bot1.Hand.The Sackville-Bagginses.Cast
Bot1.Choose(Clue Token)
[Bot1.Main2]

